description:
The types are given: an `enum` for the kind of shape and a tagged union for its measurements. Write the functions in `solution.c`:

```c
enum shape_kind { CIRCLE, RECTANGLE, TRIANGLE };

typedef struct {
    enum shape_kind kind;
    union {
        struct { double radius; } circle;
        struct { double width, height; } rectangle;
        struct { double a, b, c; } triangle;     /* the three side lengths */
    };
} Shape;

const char *kind_name(enum shape_kind kind);  /* "circle", "rectangle", "triangle" */
double area(const Shape *s);                  /* a triangle's area by Heron's formula */
double perimeter(const Shape *s);
Shape make_square(double side);               /* a RECTANGLE */
```

Heron's formula: with `p = (a + b + c) / 2`, the area is `sqrt(p (p - a) (p - b) (p - c))`. `M_PI` is not part of standard C, so write pi out: `3.14159265358979323846`. Use a `switch` on the kind.

